    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **34 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string membership tier with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133).\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `membershipTier` string/enum property (which generates `OwnerDto` and its `MembershipTierEnum`) with an integer `membershipLevel`, `minimum: 1`, `maximum: 3`, documenting the new derivation.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 swapped the `membershipTier` mapping for `membershipLevel`, and replaced the tier-deriving method with:\n```java\nstatic Integer membershipLevel(Owner owner) {\n    int level = 1;\n    if (hasEmail) level++;\n    if (namesakeCount == 0) level++;\n    return Math.min(level, 3);\n}\n```\nMade it `static` so the audit step can reuse it, keeping the formula single-sourced. (The old GOLD/household logic is gone \u2014 level no longer depends on `householdMemberCount`; level 4 is reserved for tenure.)\n\n**`src/main/java/.../owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel=...` (via the shared `OwnerMapper.membershipLevel`) instead of any tier.\n\n**Stale comments** \u2014 removed the \"yields the 'GOLD' membership tier\" references in `owners.POST.yml` and `AssignHouseholdMemberCount.java`.\n\nThe four relevant acceptance tests (Cp15 tier\u2192level replacement, Cp21 audit records level, Cp23 no GOLD for households, Cp24 numeric level cap) and all 34 tests pass.",
